#!/bin/sh
# The full suite, under the lock, before anything leaves this machine.
#
# There is no hosted CI and there is not going to be (CLAUDE.md). So the last
# check before a push is this one, and it is the only thing standing between a
# broken commit and four other sessions pulling it. On 21 Sep 2026 a broken
# uncommitted migration took 22 test files down across every session on this
# machine; a commit that does it is worse, because it travels.
#
# `npm test` takes the suite lock itself, so two sessions pushing at once queue
# rather than fight over the database.
#
# Never `--no-verify`. If the suite is wrong, fix the suite.
set -e

root=$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)
cd "$root/apps/api"

echo "pre-push: running the API suite (takes the lock; another session's run will make this wait)…"
if npm test --silent; then
  echo "pre-push: green — pushing."
  exit 0
fi

cat >&2 <<'MSG'

pre-push: the suite failed, so nothing was pushed.

  · Run `npm run test:files -- test/<file>.test.js` to look at one file.
  · Failures spread across many database-backed files usually mean another
    session is running its own suite — the lock should prevent that, so check
    for a stale one at $TMPDIR/epic-suite.lock.
  · If a migration of yours is uncommitted, the test database does not have it:
    commit it with the tests that need it.

MSG
exit 1
